							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">I can picture it exactly how he tells it.... it&#039;s cold blooded.<br /><br />I&#039;ve sen the cops around ANYTHING taht&#039;s hiphop take actions before asking questions...<br /><br />It&#039;s unfortunate that the SPD still feel that Hiphop music supports a negative enviroment.<br /><br />So from the jump cops think everybody in the area of something involving Urban Arts are going to &quot;interfere&quot; with their business.<br /><br />That&#039;s why the best weapon we as a community (when these types of things happen) can use, is a camera phone, or something of the sort with a video camera option on it....<br /><br />I was infront of Tommy&#039;s awhile back, and one of our friends &quot;Graham&quot; got hemmed up by 2 bike cops that abruptly wanted to clear all the crowd smoking infront of the club... so as soon as he got grabbed by the female cop... 3 people pulled out their camera phones, and were about 8 feet from Graham (pushed up against the wall) video&#039;ing the whole thing going down.... <br /><br />Needless to say, the police saw us video recording it with our phones, and they may have been treating him a little less rough. <br /><br />It&#039;s sad that we have to take these precautions when dealing wit our own &quot;PROTECTORS&quot;.... but first things first....<br /><br />Protect yourself from them (sometimes).... Especially when you&#039;re upset with the way the handle a situation that is petty, but escalates into something ridiculous.<br /><br /></div>
